The '''Mesogean Sea''' is a sea connected to the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] surrounded by the Mesogean region and almost completely enclosed by land: on the north by [[Southern Kaftia]], on the south by [[Northern Illypnia]]. The sea is sometimes considered a part of the Neptic Ocean, although it is usually identified as a separate body of water. The name Mesogean is derived from the [[wikipedia:Greek language|Aetolian]] ''Mesogeios'' (Μεσόγειος), from μέσο, "middle" + γη, "land, earth"). It covers an approximate area of 3.07 million km². 

